# Implementation Workflow Enforcement

When engaging with [Docs/Implementation.md](mdc:Docs/Implementation.md):

- Treat the work as a continuous, end-to-end task spanning all stages in the document.
- Do not stop or pause between stages; proceed sequentially until all stages are completed or a hard blocker is encountered.
- Create and maintain a structured todo list per stage; mark items complete as you finish them.
- Follow project rules and priorities from:
  - [Docs/Bug_tracking.md](mdc:Docs/Bug_tracking.md)
  - [Docs/Implementation.md](mdc:Docs/Implementation.md)
  - [Docs/project_structure.md](mdc:Docs/project_structure.md)
  - [Docs/UI_UX_doc.md](mdc:Docs/UI_UX_doc.md)
- Use yarn for all commands; ensure no existing node processes are running before `yarn dev`.
- Prefer Amplify Gen 2 sandbox for local backend; Amplify hosting for production.
- Only stop early if:
  - A required human decision is explicitly needed, or
  - A critical, external blocker prevents further progress.

On completion of all stages:
- Reconcile and close the todo list.
- Ensure no errors or warnings remain and that UI/UX matches specifications where applicable.
- Document any bugs and resolutions in [Docs/Bug_tracking.md](mdc:Docs/Bug_tracking.md).
